The modern conception of goblins and orcs as races of evil humanoids
originated with Tolkien. The Oxford English Dictionary defines "goblin"
as "a mischievous and ugly demon" and the examples it gives show that
it was also used as a synoun for "faerie".

On the other hand, "orc" is either a sea monster (same as modern
"orca") or a synoun for "ogre".


